<title>FRANCE: Cascades slips into the red in 1996.</title>
<headline>Cascades slips into the red in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net				  loss 11.7   vs  profit 105.3</p>
<p>    Operating				 61.1   vs	   101.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional     loss  1.7   vs  profit  30.1</p>
<p>    Cashflow				  98.2   vs	   119.2</p>
<p>    Turnover			     1,424.0   vs	 1,566.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Paper producer Cascades published the figures in a statement.</p>
<p>It said turnover was down 9.1 percent due to lower pulp prices. But it said the cardboard market had shown signs of recovery in early 1997, leading the group to expect an improvement in this year's results.</p>
<p>A recovery in the pulp market is also expected during the year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
